Finding dips at finite azimuthal separations suggested the losses were due to crossing tracks, and not genuinely merged tracks. This hypothesis was taken further by considering the radial crossing point of tracks with particular momenta and azimuthal separation. The schematic representation in figure 5.9 illustrates the range of azimuthal separations of a pair that results in a crossing point within the active region of a TPC sector. The trigger and associated track momenta are 3.0 and 1.0 GeV/c respectively. Below these diagrams the limits are shown superposed over a correlation formed using tracks with similar transverse momenta. A qualitative correspondence is seen between the dip width and the affected range.

